// THE FOOD COURT — BOOGALOO — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// THE FOOD COURT as a 1966 Latin boogaloo — a game alternate of hub, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "some groovy new remixes for the food court". BOOGALOO is Spanish Harlem's Latin soul —
// Joe Cuba Sextet's "Bang Bang", Pete Rodriguez's "I Like It Like That", Willie Bobo: a piano
// montuno, a tumbao bass, congas, timbales, bongos, cowbell, handclaps on the backbeat, the
// vibraphone, short horns, a funky clean guitar, and the room shouting "HEY!".
// 
// THE HOOK is THE FOOD COURT's own lead (hub.js bars 13–28) note for note: the sixteenth arpeggio
// A C E C | E G B G | G B D B | D F♯ A F♯ ‖ … | B D F D, on the vibes at the hub's octave-up pitch
// in the heads and an octave above that in the chant; the clean guitar doubles it in 21–24 (at the
// hub's own pitch) and 37–40. THE HARMONY is the hub's at the montuno's half-bar rate:
//   | Am9 · Gmaj9 (its beat 4 the arpeggio's D) | Am9 · G6/9 · E7♭9 |   (the B–D–F = rootless E7♭9)
//   the descarga: the dorian | Am9 | D9 | vamp the hub's D major implies; a hemiola break on D9 · E7♭9.
// THE LANDMARKS: 90 bpm (the Trophy Room's toaster parade dances at hub.js's bpm); an 8-bar intro
// heard on the walk-in, then the loop from bar 9 (hub.js's loop start), no select loop (hub.js has
// none); no TNGR-2 (the Food Court entry warms MRDR-3 / worklet lanes only); the `bass` lane
// carries the tumbao; the 2-3 clave runs unbroken over the 32-bar loop.
// 
//   1–4    THE DOORS — the piano montuno alone, then the shell of the timbales and the güiro (2), the tumbao and the congas (3); a timbale fill, a horn stab and the room's "HEY!" into
//   5–8    THE BAND — the kit, handclaps on 2 and 4, bongos on the martillo, the clean guitar's chank, the horns' first hit and a mambo figure; "HEY!" into the loop
//   9–16   HEAD A (the loop starts) — THE FOOD COURT's arpeggio on the vibes, cross-stick, cascara on the timbale shell, bongos; GUITAR 1 chops in at 13; horn "bap-baps" at the phrase ends
//   17–24  HEAD B — the band opens up: snare backbeat, the cowbell, the horns' mambo answering the vibes; in 21–24 the clean guitar doubles the hook at the hub's own pitch and the hub's own "hey!" (its vox lane) returns on the & of 2; a gliss into
//   25–28  DESCARGA — the jam on | Am9 | D9 |: a vibes solo over the "Oye Cómo Va" montuno, cascara, güiro, the guitars in open Am7 / D9
//   29–31  DESCARGA — the percussion: a timbale solo, the congas pushed, handclaps on the clave, the cowbell, the horns' moña riff
//   32–32  THE BREAK — the whole band on a hemiola, D9 · E7♭9 every three sixteenths, an abanico roll, "HEY!", a piano gliss into
//   33–40  THE PARTY CHANT — the hook an octave up on the vibes (the clean guitar under it from 37), the room calling "FOOD COURT!" and answering "HEY!", the horns on every change, the full kit and the bells; bar 40 turns back to bar 9
// 
// Sounds: the vibes (mrdrVibraphone, bright: exciter); the piano montuno (mrdrPopGrand), its gliss
// on the hub's keyGliss lane; GUITAR 1 frppFunkRhythm chops (Alternate-down strum, parity asserted),
// GUITAR 2 frppCleanElectric open-chord chank (down strum) and the hook; the horn section
// (mrdrHornStab) in three-part stabs; the tumbao on frppBassNeck over a sine; the Breakbeat kit;
// two pairs of handclaps (clap808, Velvet Basement); congas (slap, open, tumba, heel-tip), bongos;
// song-local timbales (macho, hembra, rimshot, paila) and güiro (long, short); the cowbell
// (cbSosTriangle); the gang "HEY!" and the "FOOD COURT!" call on song-local JMJR-4 speakers;
// the hub's own engine "hey!" (vox) in 21–24. No CRLS-1, no TNGR-2, no PWM.
// 
// Levels measured (solo LUFS through the master chain, _remix-bounce --lanes --range), 25 Oct:
//   chant 33–40   vibes −25.7 (the top), bass −27.9, kick −28.5, piano and horns ~5 under the vibes,
//                 snare −34.5, claps −37 a pair, congas −37.6, the gang −34.6, the call −35.7,
//                 hats −39.5, maracas −41.6, cowbell −40.1
//   head A 9–16   vibes the loudest melodic part over the cross-stick, cascara and bongos
//   descarga I    the vibes solo −27.4 over kick −28.8, bass −30.7, piano −33.2, güiro ~20 under
//   bands: low-mid +5 and air −5 against the cabinet median — an acoustic band with the vibes and
//   the montuno in 300–800 Hz; the montuno has a −4.5 dB dip at 380 Hz, the vibes are left bright.
// Trailing master gain -6.6 dB: −24.1 LUFS integrated, peak −5.1 dBFS (the hub's menu line, −24).
// 40 bars at 90, straight, 107 s; the loop 9–40 is 85 s.
// Written by work/local/_hub-remix-boogaloo.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs, which self-checks
// chord tones, chromatic notes as resolving approaches only, semitone clashes between every pair of
// sounding parts, one note per string in hand shapes, the strum parity, the loop wrap and the
// landmarks; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
